h2. 🔗 Common Use Cases

|| Team || Use Case ||
| SRE | Incident enrichment and routing |
| Platform | Identify noisy services/resources |
| APM | Analyze slow or failing transactions |
| Infra | CPU/memory/disk anomaly investigation |
| Security | Detect unusual activity patterns |
| DevOps | Trigger CI/CD or rollback pipelines |

---

h2. 🔀 Standard Decision Flow

IF critical → PagerDuty  
ELSE IF warning → Slack  
ELSE → Log only  

---

h2. 🛠️ Reusable Workflow Templates

*1. Alert Enrichment*
- Trigger → Alert
- Query → Add context
- Action → Send enriched notification

*2. Root Cause Analysis*
- Trigger → Alert
- Query → Identify impacted entities
- Condition → Filter top offenders
- Action → Notify

*3. Multi-Entity Analysis*
- Trigger → Alert
- Query → Get list
- Loop → Analyze each
- Action → Notify or aggregate

*4. Auto-Remediation*
- Trigger → Alert
- Query → Validate issue
- Condition → Confirm severity
- Action → Call API / Lambda

---

h2. 🧠 Best Practices

- Always enrich alerts with context (entity, metric, timeframe)
- Optimize NRQL queries (use LIMIT, filters)
- Use conditions to reduce alert noise
- Handle empty query results gracefully
- Keep workflows simple and modular

---

h2. ⚠️ Common Mistakes

|| Mistake || Impact ||
| No conditions | Alert fatigue |
| Heavy queries in loops | Slow workflows |
| No context in alerts | Poor usability |
| Too many steps | Hard to maintain |

---

h2. 📊 Workflow vs Alert

|| Feature || Alert || Workflow ||
| Simple threshold | Yes | No |
| Multi-step logic | No | Yes |
| Data enrichment | No | Yes |
| Automation | No | Yes |

---

h2. 🎯 Key Takeaways

- Workflow Automation = Smart Alerting + Automation
- Use it for multi-step, data-driven workflows
- Works across all teams (SRE, APM, Infra, Security, DevOps)
- Focus on actionable, context-rich outputs